Figure 5 illustrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the transport of antigens to draining lymph nodes. Specifically, Nano-11 formulations lead to a greater mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of ovalbumin (OVA) within OVA-containing cells in the lymph nodes on both Day 1 and Day 2, surpassing OVA alone and aluminum hydroxide (AH) formulations. Furthermore, Nano-11 increases the percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among OVA-positive cells, indicating more efficient targeting and delivery of adsorbed antigens to these immunopotentiating cells compared to other vaccine formulations.